pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer B excludes the line-ending commit and credits Sam Okafor with no lines. It does not mention Noor Haddad or Kofi Mensah, and it does not treat bots as people. Nothing in it is a fail condition.\",\"pass\":true}],\n\"C\": [{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer C calls Paul Borman the main author of time.go by commit count, with no line share. It says he is gone, but it lists Sam Okafor as a time.go author with a recent change.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer C credits Mei Chen with the Time7 accessor but gives no share for her. It gives no MikeWang share either, and lists Ravi Menon first as the latest author.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer C follows the sql.go to database_sql.go history and lists the original authors as gone. It gives no percentage and does not name Overfelt as the largest author.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer C names Ravi, Rowe and Kofi as recently active, and treats Rowe as one person via the mailmap. It gives no repo-wide share of lines owned by departed people and no per-file active shares. It also treats Mei Chen as a possible contact.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer C flags Kofi Mensah's 1970 date as a bad timestamp, but says it cannot tell when he was last active. It lists Sam Okafor among time.go authors with a recent change, though not as an owner.\",\"pass\":false}],\n\"D\": [{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer D credits Sam Okafor with 100% of time.go by blame. It then says that is misleading, but it gives no line share for Paul Borman.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives MikeWang 101 of 117 lines (86%), which is outside the 72–90% range only if counted wrongly, but 86% is inside it. It credits Mei Chen with the Time7 accessor and says Ravi's and Mei's changes were small. It gives no share for Mei.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer D follows the history of database_sql.go and names Justin Overfelt (26 of 59 lines) as the largest author. It also names Andrew Stone, Wheeler and Souza, and says none of them is active. It says Ravi only did the rename.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer D does not give the 95.9% repo-wide figure. It says nobody has committed in the last 90 days, which is wrong because Ravi's 2026-06-17 commit is the last one. It also lists Mei Chen as a reviewer.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer D names Sam Okafor as the 'main author by blame' of time.go with 100%. It then flags that as misleading, but it still presents him in the table as the owner. It also lists Kofi Mensah's 1970 date as a timestamp oddity.\",\"pass\":false}],\n\"E\": [{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer E says blame credits Sam Okafor with 100% but calls that misleading. It lists Paul Borman as the real author with 'last commit 2021'. It gives no line share for him, so the 65–80% requirement is not met.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives MikeWang 86% of version7.go and credits Mei Chen with Time7 at 9%. It says Ravi wrote only the step-back docs. It does not credit Ravi with Mei's lines.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer E follows sql.go to database_sql.go and names Justin Overfelt at 44%. It names Andrew Stone, Daniel Souza and David E. Wheeler, and says all are inactive. It says Ravi only did the rename.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer E says most authors are gone but gives no 95.9% figure. It says Ravi touched version7.go and treats Rowe as possibly two identities. It does not name Kofi as active, and it gives no per-file active shares.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer E says Sam Okafor's ownership is misleading because of the line-ending commit. It treats Kofi's 1970 date as a bad timestamp but does not call him active. It does not mention Noor Haddad. Kofi is not shown as active, which the criterion requires.\",\"pass\":false}],\n\"F\": [{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer F says Paul Borman wrote almost all of time.go and